{
  "title": "Hip Biomechanics",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/recon/9064/hip-biomechanics",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 26 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Joint Biomechanics Definitions",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Joint reaction force defined as force generated within a joint in response to forces acting on the joint",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "in the hip, it is the result of the need to **balance the moment arms** of the body weight and abductor tension",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "maintains a **level pelvis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Coupled forces",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "when two movements and associated forces are coupled",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Joint congruence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "relates to fit of two articular surfaces",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "high congruence increases joint contact area",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Instant center of rotation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "point about which a joint rotates",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often changes during rotation due to joint translation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "center of gravity of human is just **anterior to S2**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Friction and lubrication",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "not a function of contact area",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "lubrication decreases friction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "examples",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "coefficient of friction of **human joints is .002 to .04**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "TJA (metal on PE) **is .05 to .15**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Free Body Analysis Definitions",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Newtons laws",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "first law",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "if there is no net force on an object, its velocity remains constant",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "second law",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "force equals mass multiplied by acceleration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**F=ma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "third law",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "when a first body exerts a force on a second body, the second body exerts a force that is equal in magnitude and opposite in direction on the first body",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**F2=-F1**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Force",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "definition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a push or pull on an object resulting from the object's interaction with another object",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "equation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**force = mass x acceleration, F=ma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**1 Newton = force required to give 1 kg mass an acceleration of 1 m/s2**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Vector",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "definition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "a quantity that contains both direction and magnitude",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "scalar quantities do not have direction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "forces and velocity can be broken down into vectors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moment (torque)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "definition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the tendency of a force to rotate a body around an axis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "equation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**moment (torque) = force(perpendicular) X distance**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Work",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "definition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "when a force acts upon an object to create displacement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "equation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**work = force (vector parallel to displacement) x distance**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Energy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "definition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ability of an object to perform work",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "classification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "potential energy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "equation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**U (potential energy) = mass x gravity x height**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "kinetic energy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "equation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**KE (kinetic energy) = 1/2mv2**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hip Free Body Analysis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Free body analysis diagram",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "W = gravitational force",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "weight of the body minus weight of ipsilateral extremity (or **5/6 body weight**)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "M = abductor muscle force",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "R = joint reaction force",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can reach 3 to 6 times body weight",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Solving for joint reaction force (R)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "step 1: calculate My",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "principle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "the sum of all moments must be zero",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "in this case, the moments are created by My (abductor moment) and W (bodyweight moment)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "equation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**(A x My) = (B x W)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "assume A = 5cm and B = 12.5cm (this information will be given to you)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "My = 2.5W",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "step 2: calculate Ry (vertical component of joint reactive force)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Ry = My + W**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Ry = 2.5W + W",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Ry = 3.5W",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "step 3: calculate R (total joint reactive force)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**R = Ry / (cos 30°)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "R = 3.5W / (cos 30°)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "R = ~4W",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Clinical Implications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Actions that **decrease joint reaction force** include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "increase in ratio of A/B (shift **center of rotation** medially)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "acetabular side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "moving acetabular component medial, inferior, and anterior",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "femoral side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "increasing offset of femoral component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "long stem prosthesis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lateralization of greater trochanter",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "by using increased offset neck/prosthesis",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**varus** neck-shaft angulation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "increases **shear** across joint",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "patient's gait",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**shifting body weight over affected hip**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "this results in Trendelenburg gait",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/9064/images/trendelenburg.jpg",
                              "caption": "trendelenburg gait"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "cane in contralateral hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "reduces abductor muscle pull and decreases the moment arm between the center of gravity and the femoral head",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "carrying load in ipsilateral hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "produces additional downward moment on same side of rotational point",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Actions that **increase joint reaction force** include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**valgus** neck-shaft angulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreases shear across joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
